            "review_title": "Review at Thanh Tuyen 3",
            "review_text": "Jinkster22\nMelbourne, Australia98 contributions\n0\nA Great Find\nMar 2013 • Couples\nAfter having a horrendous experience at a popular large seafood restaurant the night before, we were desperate to finish our Nha Trang visit on a good note so we went 'hunting' for a good seafood meal. We were staying in the tourist part of town and we decided to walk out of the area along the beachfront road (Tran Phu Street), where we came across a small unassuming restaurant named Thanh Tuyen 3 that had a good selection of seafood displayed on a table out front. The seafood looked very fresh and the staff seemed very friendly, but even though the open front restaurant didn't look all that special (very basic chairs and tables) we decided to chance it. The beers were very cold (and cheap) and we settled on a plate of bbq squid (150K), fried rice with seafood, and steamed lobster with chilli and garlic (700K/Kg) - all dishes were perfectly cooked and tasted fantastic - even without the MSG as we had asked. The service was excellent with the waiter even offering advice on what sauces to have with what dish, as well as keeping up the cold beers without asking. The prices of the drinks and dishes were less than you would pay at many other similar restaurants and the service was just great. This restaurant was a great find on the fringe of the tourist/backpacker area and made our last night in Nha Trang special.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten May 20, 2013",
